      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we align each spec/conf offset to its type\u0027s alignment when laying out the slot (and include the padding in slot_size)? For an IPv4 template with MARK + RSS, the current layout puts the RSS configuration at byte 188: the 4-byte MARK shifts it off the 8-byte alignment required by dpdk_action_rss_data/rte_flow_action_rss. init_slot_compound_actions and dpdk_flow_update_slot_actions then dereference a misaligned struct. A UBSAN probe with the installed DPDK types reproduces the invalid access. Aligning only the beginning/end of the slot does not protect these interior objects.",
      "tag": "prview:5b3d88a03f5f9a181dd5f726a37a69e9:cb480071cc737350191cf7d1d6ded5ca0766d261",
      "revId": "cb480071cc737350191cf7d1d6ded5ca0766d261",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
