      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T15:25:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we cast the left operand to uword before shifting, as max_pow2() does? The literal 1 is a 32-bit int, so this new uword helper has undefined behavior for inputs \u003e\u003d 2^31 and cannot round 64-bit values correctly. A probe calling the actual header\u0027s min_pow2((uword)1 \u003c\u003c 32) returns 1 instead of 4294967296 and triggers UBSAN\u0027s shift-exponent error. Use `(uword) 1 \u003c\u003c min_log2(x)`.",
